[Id "queens-gambit-declined"]
[Name "Queen's Gambit Declined"]
[Side "black"]
[ECO "D30-D69"]
[Description "Hold the centre with …d5 and …e6, develop quietly and castle: the classical answer to the Queen's Gambit."]
[Tags "solid, positional"]

1. d4 d5 2. c4 e6 {…e6 supports d5 solidly; the price is a passive c8 bishop for now.} 3. Nc3
  (3. Nf3 {@variation 3.Nf3} 3... Nf6 4. g3 {@variation Catalan (g3)}
    (4. Nc3 {@variation 3.Nf3} 4... Be7 {…Be7: the same position as 3.Nc3 Nf6 4.Nf3 Be7.}
{@line id=queens-gambit-declined-3nf3 level=1 tier=side name="3.Nf3 move order" summary="3.Nf3 and 4.Nc3 reach the normal QGD: develop with …Nf6 and …Be7."}
)
  4... Be7 5. Bg2 O-O 6. O-O dxc4 {…dxc4 takes the pawn now that White has castled; Black plays …a6 and …b5 or …c5 next.}
{@line id=queens-gambit-declined-catalan level=1 tier=main name="Catalan (4.g3)" summary="Against the Catalan, develop and castle, then take on c4 and hold the pawn or hit back with …c5."}
)
  (3. cxd5 {@variation Exchange} 3... exd5 (3... Qxd5 {@mistake Nc3 gains time on your queen.}) 4. Nc3 Nf6 {…Nf6 develops; Bg5 and e3 usually follow.} (4... c6 {@alt})
{@line id=queens-gambit-declined-3cxd5 level=1 tier=side name="3.cxd5" summary="After an early cxd5, take back with the pawn and develop …Nf6, …Be7 and castle."}
)
3... Nf6 4. Bg5 {@variation Orthodox (4.Bg5)}
  (4. Nf3 {@variation 4.Nf3} 4... Be7 {…Be7 develops and prepares to castle.} 5. Bf4
    (5. Bg5 O-O 6. e3 h6 7. Bh4 b6 {…b6: the same Tartakower set-up as after 4.Bg5. [%cal Gc8b7]}
{@line id=queens-gambit-declined-nf3-bg5 level=2 tier=main name="4.Nf3 Be7 5.Bg5" summary="5.Bg5 reaches the Orthodox QGD: castle, …h6 and …b6, as always."}
)
  5... O-O 6. e3 b6 {…b6 prepares …Bb7 and …c5, the plan of the Tartakower. [%cal Gc8b7]} (6... c5 {@alt}) (6... Nbd7 {@alt})
{@line id=queens-gambit-declined-nf3-bf4 level=1 tier=main name="4.Nf3 Be7 5.Bf4" summary="Against Bf4, castle and play …b6 and …Bb7, or hit the centre with …c5."}
)
  (4. cxd5 {@variation Exchange} 4... exd5 5. Bg5 Be7 6. e3 O-O {…O-O: Black has a solid position; White usually plans the minority attack.} (6... c6 {@alt})
{@line id=queens-gambit-declined-exchange level=1 tier=main name="Exchange (4.cxd5)" summary="In the Exchange, develop …Be7 and castle; …c6, …Nbd7 and …Re8 make a solid set-up."}
7. Bd3 h6 {…h6 asks the g5 bishop to make a decision before Black finishes developing. [%cal Gh6g5]} (7... c6 {@alt}) 8. Bh4 c6 {…c6 supports d5; …Nbd7 and …Re8 come next.}
{@line id=queens-gambit-declined-exchange-bd3 level=2 tier=main name="Exchange: 7.Bd3" summary="Against Bd3, ask the bishop with …h6, then …c6, …Nbd7 and …Re8."}
)
  (4. e3 {@variation 4.e3} 4... Be7 5. Nf3 O-O {…O-O: the solid set-up again; …b6 or …c5 next.}
{@line id=queens-gambit-declined-e3 level=2 tier=main name="4.e3" summary="Against the quiet 4.e3, develop with …Be7 and castle."}
)
  (4. Bf4 {@variation 4.Bf4} 4... Be7 5. e3 O-O {…O-O, with …c5 or …b6 to follow.} (5... c5 {@alt})
{@line id=queens-gambit-declined-bf4 level=2 tier=side name="4.Bf4" summary="Against 4.Bf4, develop and castle; …c5 is a good way to hit back."}
)
4... Be7 {…Be7 breaks the pin on the f6 knight.} 5. e3
  (5. Nf3 O-O 6. e3 h6 7. Bh4 b6 {…b6: the usual Tartakower set-up, whatever White's move order.}
{@line id=queens-gambit-declined-5nf3 level=2 tier=side name="Orthodox: 5.Nf3" summary="5.Nf3 instead of 5.e3 changes nothing: castle, …h6 and …b6."}
)
5... O-O 6. Nf3 h6 {…h6 asks the bishop to decide.} (6... Nbd7 {@alt}) 7. Bh4 b6 {…b6 prepares …Bb7: the Tartakower set-up. [%cal Gc8b7]}
{@line id=queens-gambit-declined-tartakower level=1 tier=main name="Tartakower (7…b6)" summary="The Orthodox QGD: …Be7, castle, …h6, then …b6 and …Bb7 to solve the problem bishop."}
8. cxd5
  (8. Bd3 Bb7 {…Bb7 develops the bishop to its best diagonal; …dxc4 and …c5 can follow.}
{@line id=queens-gambit-declined-tartakower-bd3 level=2 tier=side name="Tartakower: 8.Bd3" summary="Against 8.Bd3, finish the plan with …Bb7, then …dxc4 or …c5."}
)
8... Nxd5 {…Nxd5 trades pieces to free Black's game.} 9. Bxe7 Qxe7 {…Qxe7 recaptures; …Bb7 and …c5 come next.} (9... Nxe7 {@alt})
{@line id=queens-gambit-declined-tartakower-cxd5 level=2 tier=main name="Tartakower: 8.cxd5" summary="After cxd5, take back with the knight and trade pieces; then …Bb7 and …c5."} *
